# Vivado Simulation Environment

## Overview

This directory contains the Vivado simulation environment for the DexterLab Command Parser.

It provides a standalone testbench environment for validating the parser together with the reference slave models and supported bus converters using XSIM (Vivado Simulator).

This README focuses only on how to run simulations.

For parser architecture, command format, response format, and bus-converter behavior, please refer to the main project documentation.

---

## Requirements

- Windows 10 / Windows 11
- Vivado 2025.1
- Vivado `settings64.bat`
- MSYS2 / MINGW64 (optional, for Makefile support)

---

## Environment Setup

Before running any simulation, activate the Vivado environment:

```bat
vivado_env.bat
```

This script loads `settings64.bat` and prepares the Vivado toolchain.

---

## Running the Simulation

### Compile, Elaborate and Run

```sh
make xsim
```

This generates:

- `xsim.dir/`
- `tb_parser_sim.wdb`
- `xsim.log`
- `xelab.log`
- Additional simulation artifacts

---

## Opening the GUI

Open the XSIM waveform viewer:

```sh
make xsim_gui
```

or manually:

```sh
xsim tb_parser_sim --gui
```

The GUI requires a previously generated simulation database (`.wdb`) and elaboration output.

---

## Debug Logging

Debug messages (`severity note`) are controlled by:

```vhdl
constant ENABLE_DEBUG_LOG : boolean := true;
```

Defined in:

```text
cmd_cfg.vhd
```

### Debug OFF

```vhdl
ENABLE_DEBUG_LOG := false;
```

- Suppresses debug messages
- Keeps warning, error and fatal messages enabled

### Debug ON

```vhdl
ENABLE_DEBUG_LOG := true;
```

- Enables parser debug output
- Useful during command flow analysis and protocol debugging

Vivado/XSIM does not support runtime severity filtering comparable to GHDL, therefore debug control is implemented directly inside the VHDL sources.

---

## Cleaning the Directory

To remove generated simulation files:

```sh
make clean
```

This removes:

- `xsim.dir/`
- `.pb` files
- `.jou` files
- `.log` files
- `.wdb` files
- Other temporary simulation artifacts

---

## Supported Verification Targets

The simulation environment is used to validate:

- Core parser functionality
- Command decoding
- Response generation
- WAIT / POLL / PING / DUMP mechanisms
- SINGLE command execution
- BURST command execution
- FIFO command execution
- WRAP address handling
- Timeout detection
- Error handling and reporting
- AXI-Full bus converter
- AXI-Lite bus converter
- AHB-Full bus converter
- AHB-Lite bus converter

---

## Simulation Inputs

The regression environment uses:

| File | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| cmd.txt | Command sequence used by the parser regression |
| ram_init.cde | Initial contents of the reference RAM model |

The command file may contain:

- SINGLE accesses
- BURST accesses
- FIFO operations
- WRAP operations
- WAIT commands
- POLL commands
- DUMP commands
- Error-injection tests

---

## Generated Outputs

The Vivado simulation environment produces:

- Simulation transcript logs
- XSIM waveform database (`.wdb`)
- Execution statistics
- Command execution summary
- Regression pass/fail report

A successful regression typically ends with:

```text
TOTAL EXEC ERRORS = 0
TOTAL ERRORS = 0
SIMULATION RESULT: OK
```

